NNAAMMEE
     bbeeeepp — play a beep sound

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     bbeeeepp [--FF _f_r_e_q_u_e_n_c_y] [--DD _d_u_r_a_t_i_o_n___m_s] [--rr _s_a_m_p_l_e___r_a_t_e___h_z] [--dd _o_s_s___d_e_v_i_c_e]
          [--gg _g_a_i_n] [--BB] [--hh]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The bbeeeepp utility is used to playback a beep on the soundcard.

     The options are as follows:

     --FF         Sets the center frequency of the beep in Hz.  The default is
                440 Hz .

     --DD         Sets the duration of the beep in milliseconds.  The default is
                150 ms .

     --dd         Sets the soundcard to use.  The default is /dev/dsp .

     --rr         Sets the soundcard samplerate in Hz.  The default is 48000 Hz.

     --gg         Sets the waveform gain, between 0 and 100 inclusively.  The
                default is 75.

     --BB         Runs the bbeeeepp utility in the background.

     --hh         Display summary of options.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Playback default beep sound using /dev/dsp .

           $ beep

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     mixer(3), sound(4)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The bbeeeepp utility first appeared in FreeBSD 14.0.

